Subject: drm/nouveau/fifo/nv04: rate limit the CACHE_ERROR and DMA_PUSHER storms

nv04_fifo_intr_cache_error() handles one CACHE1 entry per interrupt -- it
reads the method at GET, reports it, then advances GET by four. Draining a
full cache therefore emits one error line per queued method, hundreds of them
back to back, with nothing limiting the rate.

On a single core machine that is enough to livelock the box on its own, and
with netconsole configured every one of those lines is a synchronous UDP
packet. Captured on a GeForce 7600 GS in a Pentium 4, the last thing the
kernel ever said was:

  fifo: CACHE_ERROR - ch 3 [glxgears] subc 7 mthd 1f0c data 3e87a5f8   (x N)
  clocksource: Long readout interval, skipping watchdog check: cs_nsec: 4795566857

A 4.8 second stall, and then nothing. The machine had to be power cycled.

The reporting is incidental here; the register writes below it are what
actually recovers the FIFO, and they still run for every entry. Rate limiting
only the message keeps the recovery intact and keeps the machine alive.
nvkm_error_ratelimited() already exists for exactly this.

nv04_fifo_intr_dma_pusher() floods the same way from the same class of event
and gets the same treatment.

Measured on the reference machine: ten rounds of unthrottled glxgears, seven
of which stalled the engine. Before, the first storm took the machine down
hard with no oops and no further kernel output. After, 478 callbacks
suppressed, the X server dies and respawns each time, and the box is still
running. The underlying engine stall is untouched -- this is about surviving
it.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/fifo/nv04.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/fifo/nv04.c
@@ nv04_fifo_intr_cache_error()
 	if (!(pull0 & 0x00000100) ||
 	    !nv04_fifo_swmthd(device, chid, mthd, data)) {
 		chan = nvkm_chan_get_chid(&fifo->engine, chid, &flags);
-		nvkm_error(subdev, "CACHE_ERROR - "
+		nvkm_error_ratelimited(subdev, "CACHE_ERROR - "
 			   "ch %d [%s] subc %d mthd %04x data %08x\n",
 			   chid, chan ? chan->name : "unknown",
 			   (mthd >> 13) & 7, mthd & 0x1ffc, data);
 		nvkm_chan_put(&chan, flags);
 	}
@@ nv04_fifo_intr_dma_pusher()
-		nvkm_error(subdev, "DMA_PUSHER - "
+		nvkm_error_ratelimited(subdev, "DMA_PUSHER - "
 			   ...
